From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 20:01:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: Run the Mesa sensor in
 SPI mode 1 again

The 1.617 J604 &mesa override deleted the T8132 node's spi-cpol and set
spi-cpha: the ADT names the J604's sensor "R3", J613's generation, which
runs in SPI mode 1, not the mode 2 the T8132 node defaults to for J713's
V3 sensor. The 7.3 integration folded the J604 DT overrides into
t8132-j604-lab.dtsi by property, which keeps spi-cpha but cannot carry the
deletion, so the 7.3 J604 DTB has both and binds the sensor in mode 3:

  apple-mesa spi0.0: sep sensor: bound, 8000000 Hz, mode 3 (CPOL=1 CPHA=1)
  apple_sep 3aa600000.sep: sensor gated: all 4 wake reads returned
  sixteen zero bytes. Power was cycled. CS timing: HARDWARE ...

With the 1.617 DTB the same 7.3 kernel binds mode 1 and the sensor
answers. Delete spi-cpol and set spi-cpha in the J604 board file again.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
index 12d2680006..ac6ce8aed4 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
@@ -339,7 +339,15 @@
 	};
 };
 
+/*
+ * Touch ID: the ADT names the J604's Mesa sensor "R3", J613's generation, so
+ * it runs in J613's SPI mode 1 (spi-cpha), not the mode 2 (spi-cpol) the
+ * T8132 node defaults to for J713's V3 sensor. In mode 3 (both) every wake
+ * read returns sixteen zero bytes and apple_sep gates the sensor.
+ */
 &mesa {
+	/delete-property/ spi-cpol;
+	spi-cpha;
 	/*
 	 * Per-device factory data from this Mac's own iBoot system container:
 	 * the calibration, and the signed root key the nonce session loads.
-- 
2.43.0

